{
  "A number field: arrow keys, PageUp / PageDown and spin buttons that repeat while held, bounds, a step without float noise, a format for display (currency, percent) and typing in the locale’s own way.": "",
  "`x-model` binds a number (`null` when empty). Created with `new`, the same properties are set programmatically.": "",
  "Steps and keys": "",
  "Up / Down add `step`, PageUp / PageDown add `largeStep` (10 × `step` by default), Home / End go to `min` / `max`. Steps are added on the decimal digits, so 0.1 + 0.2 is 0.3. With `wheel`, the mouse wheel steps while the field has focus.": "",
  "Spin buttons": "",
  "Pressing a spin button steps once; holding it repeats until it is let go or a bound is reached. They sit on top of each other (`stacked`) or side by side (`inline`), or not at all.": "",
  "Format and locale": "",
  "Without focus the value shows through `Intl.NumberFormat` with `format` and `locale` (the page `lang` by default); with focus it turns into the plain number to edit. What is typed is read in that locale: `1.234,5` in Turkish, `1,234.5` in English; a `.` also works as the decimal point where it cannot be a group separator. A percent is edited as shown: 12.5 for 0.125.": "",
  "Min, max and clamp": "",
  "An entered value outside `min` / `max` is brought inside when the field is left. With `clamp={false}` it stays as typed and the range check reports it.": "",
  "Decimals and empty": "",
  "`decimals` rounds every value, the one given as well as the one entered, and shows exactly that many digits while the field is not edited (`72.50`); `format` can show them otherwise. An empty field is `null`; with `allowEmpty={false}` it gets `min` (or 0) when the field is left.": "",
  "Adds / takes away `step`.": "",
  "Adds / takes away `largeStep`.": "",
  "Goes to `min` / `max` when they are set; otherwise moves the caret.": "",
  "Enters the typed text (rounded, kept in range) and fires `onEnter`.": "",
  "With `wheel`, steps while the field has focus.": "",
  "`spinbutton` on a text `<input inputmode=\"decimal\">`, so phones show a number keyboard and any locale can be typed.": "",
  "`aria-valuenow`, `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax`, and `aria-valuetext` with the formatted value (`₺1.234,50`).": "",
  "Named “Increase” / “Decrease” from `uiLocale`; not Tab stops (the arrow keys do their job).": "",
  "The names of the spin buttons and the range messages come from `uiLocale.strings`; numbers follow `locale`.": "",
  "The field. `data-spin` while the spin buttons show, and the field attributes.": "",
  "The spin buttons; `data-layout=\"stacked\" | \"inline\"`.": "",
  "One spin button; `data-step=\"up\" | \"down\"`.": "",
  "Units: the spin buttons together (`stacked`, `inline`, `disabled`), each step (`up`, `down`, `next`, `hover`, `pressed`, `disabled`) and its glyph.": "",
  "Where the steps stand (stacked at the end, or one on each side) and in which order.": "",
  "The space around the stacked spin buttons.": "",
  "Everything else, as for TextBox.": "",
  "The number; `null` when empty. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "Bounds: steps stop there, Home / End go there, entered values are kept inside (see `clamp`), the range is checked.": "",
  "What the arrow keys, the spin buttons and the wheel add.": "",
  "What PageUp / PageDown add.": "",
  "The up and down buttons in the box.": "",
  "`stacked`: arrows on top of each other; `inline`: − and + side by side.": "",
  "The mouse wheel changes the value while the field has focus.": "",
  "How the value shows without focus: `{ style: 'currency', currency: 'TRY' }`, `{ style: 'percent' }`, `{ minimumFractionDigits: 2 }`…": "",
  "the page `lang`": "",
  "The locale of the format and of what is typed.": "",
  "Digits after the point: every value is rounded to them (half away from zero), wherever it comes from, and shown with exactly that many while the field is not edited.": "",
  "A value outside `min` / `max` is brought inside when entered; `false` leaves it to the range check.": "",
  "An empty field is `null`; `false` puts `min` (or 0) in its place when the field is left.": "",
  "`input`: the value changes as soon as the text is a whole number in range; `change`: when the field is left or Enter is pressed.": "",
  "A value or a function, like the prop. `locale` reads back the locale in use.": "",
  "The value as it shows without focus, `''` when empty.": "",
  "Adds `step` × `times`, kept within `min` / `max`.": "",
  "Takes `step` × `times` away.": "",
  "The value changed. `e`: `{ value, previousValue, byUser, source, event? }`; a held spin button reports every step.": ""
}
